reator><![CDATA[zoraniko]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>MAN. I think dead internet theory is correct, I think the adage "if it feels too good to be true" needs to be followed closely, and that nothing online is trustworthy now means after 40 years of being online, it's going to make me stop using the internet.</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/xQqo0Na</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/nOYEszJ.gif" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>FAKE.

I fell in love with this cute pup on an instagram my wife sent. I fully believed it for about a minute... then looked at the account selling the life vest, which had dozens and dozens of IDENTICAL videos with different dog breeds. 85 posts in one month. 

Impossible. The company is new, the website is sketchy, it's all social media AI Slop ad scams on instagram. it's CRAZY. But I really couldn't tell for a bit, and I'm not lazy or bad at this.

But I don't want to use the internet where you have to doubt everything for minutes at a time.</div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/hBZYGL8.png" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>If people create something with no effort, it has no value. Why would I want to be subjected to this slop without my consent?

What in the hell are platforms thinking? What are these technologists thinking... because they're ruining the internet. And one giddy bad actor can launch score of these fake website companies, exponentially destroying the usability of the internet.

When the utility of the internet is broken, and you need to spend 10 minutes figuring out if a harmless, meaningless video is real... 

It is as over as shell art. Cooked, as they say. It's pretty surreal how quickly the internet degraded. First enshittification, then organic search... but holy crap it's unusable.

Why is Silicon Valley constantly answering questions no one asked? Weirdos.</div></div>]]></description><guid>https://imgur.com/a/xQqo0Na</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[unclefishbits]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>Good Ol' Times</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/svOcBzI</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/8cs4l8p.gif" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div></div>]]></description><guid>https://imgur.com/a/svOcBzI</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[IakobZ]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>Kushner</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/XHXKvrO</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/0RMnaEc.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div></div>]]></description><guid>https://imgur.com/a/XHXKvrO</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[CruiseForLife]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>Finders keepers</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/p9DlkrK</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/3pqu7oD.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div></div>]]></description><guid>https://imgur.com/a/p9DlkrK</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[PineappleIsDeliciousOnPizzaFightMe]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>Projection</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/sF0Jlj0</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/i7Hg9Sr.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div></div>]]></description><guid>https://imgur.com/a/sF0Jlj0</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[CruiseForLife]]></dc:creator></item><item><title>Carefully Curated Crap, Vol. 941</title><link>https://imgur.com/gallery/mo3q7wV</link><description><![CDATA[<div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/myeK1HX.jpg" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>1</div><div><img alt="" src="https://i.imgur.com/EC0Ipw3.png" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;"></div><div><span></span></div><div>2</div><div><img alt="" src